-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- one text, compiled
-- Each text is read as its bytes (text-bytes: a text held as its bytes gives them, shared) and backwards,
-- the order the automaton reads it in, by an elimination of its length: step i reads the byte at
-- ℓ - 1 - i. The compiled code reads the bytes where they are; nothing is built a byte.
m-len : Word → List Word → Word
m-len a nil = a
m-len a (cons c r) = m-len (wadd a #1) r
